{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04TJ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1af96357bb9f98988796ecd0a67818df048aaebb68aa3d24da71bd8b1419861d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we start with a smooth groupoid in algebraic spaces\nand we show that the associated quotient stack is an algebraic stack.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cfb11c00769fcb2d1267dc14643e85c2a77ff7aa36e34d14af47dbbefe9a55bf", "unit_id": "tag:04TJ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04TJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$[U/R]$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal-quotient-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ac1c013f4e74eea0c19b44cfa117e4b7c598bcabc16a45f4468af7a1f8facf1a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c16baf56bf66c2fdfc85ca483af9a776f17322af532fd3e297bda4fd71ce84a7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0004>.\nThen the diagonal of <MATH_0005> is representable by algebraic spaces.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:24959d581a220d83f3e3b03d089d0a4879cc79cd8a51607628e0476ecc6c84de", "unit_id": "tag:04WZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04TJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathit{Isom}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-representable-diagonal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{bootstrap-lemma-quotient-stack-isom}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0b765cfa7a7a67e356c7b380ecd29386c26b1fa13adca3f1cd59dd68c806ddc2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f922bca82f0d34f823dac4365db65ccce0b4e20289c62eb00e5d0080e8008474", "source_text": "It suffices to show that the <MATH_0001>-sheaves are algebraic\nspaces, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nThis follows from\nBootstrap, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:37e269143e1f4ecc0f48df46f85420afa85adb0b213962229872288854eba1c3", "unit_id": "tag:04WZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04TJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}_U \\to [U/R]$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-smooth-quotient-smooth-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:23da5d5c5802a1dbbf38125dc8609b31ee017472675a64cf39150258cf1d567a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f82dec0b8c0011d536ab04ebf9f5423b2f968b51435629a93843e68a4c974740", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a smooth groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0004>.\nThen the morphism <MATH_0005> is smooth and surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b3142678e8735a05f28311b584a90eb106a5a283e217a91ecf3f8cb05a6895d1", "unit_id": "tag:04X0:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04TJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$x : (\\Sch/T)_{fppf} \\to [U/R]$", "MATH_0003": "$1$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\mathcal{S}_U \\times_{[U/R]} (\\Sch/T)_{fppf}\n\\longrightarrow\n(\\Sch/T)_{fppf}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$F \\to T$", "MATH_0007": "$T$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$T$", "MATH_0010": "$x|_{(\\Sch/T_i)_{fppf}}$", "MATH_0011": "$x_i : T_i \\to U$", "MATH_0012": "$F \\times_T T_i$", "MATH_0013": "$2$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{S}_U \\times_{[U/R]} (\\Sch/T_i)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0015": "$T_i \\to T$", "MATH_0016": "$x$", "MATH_0017": "$x : T \\to U$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n\\mathcal{S}_U \\times_{[U/R]} (\\Sch/T)_{fppf}\n=\n(\\mathcal{S}_U \\times_{[U/R]} \\mathcal{S}_U)\n\\times_{\\mathcal{S}_U} (\\Sch/T)_{fppf}\n=\n\\mathcal{S}_R \\times_{\\mathcal{S}_U} (\\Sch/T)_{fppf}\n$$", "MATH_0019": "$2$", "MATH_0020": "$F = R \\times_{s, U, x} T$", "MATH_0021": "$R \\times_{s, U, x} T \\to T$", "MATH_0022": "$s : R \\to U$", "MATH_0023": "$s$", "MATH_0024": "$e : U \\to R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-diagonal-quotient-stack}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-representable-diagonal}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{categories-lemma-2-fibre-product-erase-factor}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-lemma-quotient-stack-2-cartesian}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:493ead3036f20c5fab4a25f399bd4e34b00e892612789bc82d07d9d63e5cfb96", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e17b326eede3f474c8261f83511060add70d9b4b76fac4bcce0c8f1fa13ba455", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and let <MATH_0002>\nbe a <MATH_0003>-morphism. We have to show that the projection\n<MATH_0004>\nis surjective and smooth. We already know that the left hand side\nis representable by an algebraic space <MATH_0005>, see\nLemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nHence we have to show the corresponding morphism <MATH_0006> of\nalgebraic spaces is surjective and smooth.\nSince we are working with properties of morphisms of algebraic\nspaces which are local on the target in the fppf topology we\nmay check this fppf locally on <MATH_0007>. By construction, there exists\nan fppf covering <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009> such that\n<MATH_0010> comes from a morphism\n<MATH_0011>. (Note that <MATH_0012> represents the\n<MATH_0013>-fibre product <MATH_0014>\nso everything is compatible with the base change via <MATH_0015>.)\nHence we may assume that <MATH_0016> comes from <MATH_0017>.\nIn this case we see that\n<MATH_0018>\nThe first equality by\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0003>\nand the second equality by\nGroupoids in Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0004>.\nClearly the last <MATH_0019>-fibre product is represented by the algebraic\nspace <MATH_0020> and the projection\n<MATH_0021> is smooth as the base change of\nthe smooth morphism of algebraic spaces <MATH_0022>.\nIt is also surjective as <MATH_0023> has a section (namely the identity\n<MATH_0024> of the groupoid).\nThis proves the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fb8c53cf5e45ab3ef054a61da223ae569a8dd818c1aab0c8df9077610425b458", "unit_id": "tag:04X0:proof"}
